{"title":"1972 AHSME Problems/Problem 15","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A contractor estimated that one of his two bricklayers would take <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> hours to build a certain wall and the other <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> hours. \nHowever, he knew from experience that when they worked together, their combined output fell by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> bricks per hour. \nBeing in a hurry, he put both men on the job and found that it took exactly 5 hours to build the wall. The number of bricks in the wall was\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/5/985cf2437b787a9d35028fbb115d62826f1cca90.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A) }500\\qquad \\textbf{(B) }550\\qquad \\textbf{(C) }900\\qquad \\textbf{(D) }950\\qquad  \\textbf{(E) }960$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"443\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1972_AHSME_Problems/Problem_15&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Every hour, the contractors lay <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/1/e81f419e7b249c9968c4900441a9664634cb8242.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x/9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc5669017c9b78716ae328d9e5b6d475882b8881.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x/10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"37\" height=\"18\" /> bricks, assuming a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> bricks in the wall. Together, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/c/b9ce5b0c5f2eb11734c2314ee2d01a9a2baa7a41.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x/5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"28\" height=\"18\" /> bricks are laid per hour:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/b/d3b3473a8efa6c0209eb792d833549ec457a4010.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x = 5(x/9 + x/10 - 10)\\]\" width=\"184\" height=\"18\" />\nThere are a total of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/9/2392936e3d29df94c1b9a305bcce20fb8541165d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=900$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" /> bricks, and the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/0/9f04db1e260d4b8766670a5d67ab4a61897d763a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(C)} \\quad 900$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"71\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>-edited by coolmath34\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017105618\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.006 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.006 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 46/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 1998/5